    {
      // PROLOGUE ONLY. The scripted defeat's boss, named by PrologueScript.BuildStage and by
      // nothing in campaign.json - it is not on any stage a player can reach by playing.
      //
      // Overtuned on purpose, and that is the whole mechanism: there is no forced-outcome code
      // anywhere for the prologue loss. The fight runs through the ordinary CombatSimulation and
      // the player loses because the numbers say so, exactly like any other loss. Roughly 6x a
      // chapter-1 boss's HP and 4x its attack, against a five-body line at level 42, which loses
      // it inside the round limit by a wide margin.
      //
      // Deliberately NOT unloseable. A player who somehow survives still reaches the antagonist's
      // interrupt, because FirstRun fires that beat on the result screen regardless of outcome -
      // see the note on PrologueStep.Boss. An "impossible" fight and a story that assumes it are
      // two different promises and only one of them is safe to make.
      //
      // Appended at the end of the file on purpose: retune/ch2-late-stages has an unmerged diff
